; Leg HF -- FreeDOS for Victor on REAL hardware, COM2, 9600.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
; FIRST TIME ON REAL SILICON.  SS16az and SS16ba are MAME only.
;
; BEFORE THIS LEG, CAPTURE WHAT THE MACHINE PUTS ON THE WIRE WITH NOTHING OF
; OURS RUNNING (SS16az's method lesson -- it settled the channel question in
; 150 seconds where four counter readings had not).
;
; CONTROL: SS16az leg FDE -- 685 cps, 0 damaged packets, 0 timeouts,
; 0 resends, rxpeak 19 of 4096, rxbytes 37,569.
; Expect  v9k: dos oem=fd ver=622 irq1=09  and SS1b's direct chip-programming
; fallback, because FreeDOS's COM device carries attribute 0x8000 with no
; IOCTL bit and AX=4402h simply fails.
;
; ALSO FREE ON THIS DOS: nap per= and every tot=.  SS16ba established the
; half-second clock quantum is Victor MS-DOS 3.1's and NOT the machine's --
; not one FreeDOS figure was a multiple of 50 -- so a max= cannot be compared
; across the two DOSes.
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPHF.OUT> s16bcHF.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set speed 9600
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bcHF.pkt
send rcvhf.dat
statistics
